# .cursorrules

# Project rules for Cursor. This file is loaded automatically when Cursor opens this directory.
#
# Derived from the AGENTS.md principles in the Repo Ops Starter Pack.
# AGENTS.md remains the canonical source for repo-level rules.
# This file adapts those principles for Cursor's rules format.
#
# Keep this file concise — Cursor has a limited context budget for rules.

## Project Identity

This project is: <one-sentence description>

## Tech Stack

- <language / framework / database / package manager>

## Conventions

- Follow existing code patterns. Do not introduce new abstractions without asking.
- Prefer small, focused changes over large rewrites.
- Use <naming-convention> for variables and functions.
- Keep imports organized: <import ordering preference>.

## Workflow Rules

- Do not modify files outside the scope of the current task.
- Run tests after making code changes: `<test-command>`
- Do not commit directly to the main branch.
- Ask before: merging, deploying, deleting files or branches, changing secrets, modifying CI/CD.

## What Not To Touch

- <generated files, vendor directories, lock files>
- <paths the agent should not modify without asking>

## Code Quality

- No unrelated refactors alongside feature work.
- No dependency upgrades unless explicitly requested.
- No formatting sweeps across files not being changed.

## Context Decay

If you are losing track of constraints or repeating earlier steps, say so. The user will start a fresh session with a migration packet rather than pushing through degraded context.

## See Also

For the full repo memory (branch truth, merge conventions, deploy rules, stop-and-ask list), see AGENTS.md in the repo root.
